A page fault occurs during runtime PPR handling when SMM memory access
controls are enabled. The fault is triggered because SMM runtime code
calls GetSubChMaxStrobeValid(), which performs accesses that violate
memory protections, causing an exception when the SMM environment cannot
reach the required resources. The change captures SubChMaxStrobe earlier
in DXE and exposes it through the MEM_TOPOLOGY structure so SMM can read
a pre-populated value instead of invoking unsafe runtime helpers.

[Resolution]
Populate SubChMaxStrobe into MEM_TOPOLOGY during DXE and use
MemTopology->SubChMaxStrobe in SMM runtime instead of calling
GetSubChMaxStrobeValid() at runtime. Update initialization in
InitializeMemTopology to set SubChMaxStrobe and modify SMM routing logic
to read the value from MEM_TOPOLOGY. Add a debug log entry to verify the
populated value.

Package/Module:
ServerRasPkg

[Impacted Platform]
GRANITE RAPIDS AP,
GRANITERAPIDS SP

